00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:05.220
So Elastifile offers a
fully managed file storage

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:08.490
as a service inside
Google Cloud.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.010
We're POSIX
compliant, which means

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:14.660
that you can move enterprise
workloads, such as SAP,

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:19.290
directly to the cloud without
the need for refactoring.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:23.580
We are scalable, and this is
one of our key differentiators.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:26.550
And we'll show you this
shortly in the demo as well.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:29.460
Because we are software
defined, essentially you

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:33.540
can dynamically grow us
and shrink us upon need.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:35.190
And you are charged
by the minute.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.650
When you use more, you
pay as much as you use.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.510
When you don't need
it anymore, you

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:43.410
can just shrink it down
or close it up altogether.

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:48.320
We provide enterprise feature
sets, such as HA, snapshots,

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:50.710
dedup, compression.

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:53.010
So we really can
migrate and move

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:55.740
to working the way you
worked on prem, even

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.120
as you migrate into the cloud.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.760
And we are cloud native.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.710
