VMs that we're spinning up.

00:25:57.990 --> 00:26:01.540
And on the left, you
actually see orchestration.

00:26:01.540 --> 00:26:04.320
We are fully accessible via API.

00:26:04.320 --> 00:26:08.760
And in this case, we're using
Slurm to automate the bring up

00:26:08.760 --> 00:26:10.770
of 1,000 VMs.

00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:14.760
These are preemptible VMs,
which is another great reason

00:26:14.760 --> 00:26:16.590
to use a file service.

00:26:16.590 --> 00:26:20.370
You can save a lot by
using the preemptible VMs.

00:26:20.370 --> 00:26:22.350
If someone falls, no issue.

00:26:22.350 --> 00:26:24.930
You have persistent
storage as a service.

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:28.260
You spin up another VM
through the orchestration,

00:26:28.260 --> 00:26:31.040
and that VM will
access the data.

00:26:31.040 --> 00:26:34.770
We have just spun up
1,000 of these VMs

00:26:34.770 --> 00:26:36.390
through orchestration.

00:26:36.390 --> 00:26:39.090
And what I want you
to follow is a bit

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:43.170
of the throughput that we are
achieving and the connections.

00:26:43.170 --> 00:26:46.020
We're actually
using two NFS mounts

00:26:46.020 --> 00:26:47.700
for each one of those VMs.

00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:52.140
So you can see the count
of connections rising up.

00:26:52.140 --> 00:26:57.420
Right now at 1,300, growing
up to those 2,000 connections

00:26:57.420 --> 00:26:59.790
for those 2,000 VMs.

00:26:59.790 --> 00:27:01.740
And the throughput
we're running now

00:27:01.740 --> 00:27:05.620
is upward of 2.4
gigabytes per second.

00:27:05.620 --> 00:27:08.700
This is not the limit,
but in terms of cost,

00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:11.220
even though we're
using preemptible VMs,

00:27:11.220 --> 00:27:14.640
we didn't want to go
much beyond 1,000.

00:27:14.640 --> 00:27:17.610
You see now a tail
there of workloads,

00:27:17.610 --> 00:27:20.730
and that's actually the
orchestration system

00:27:20.730 --> 00:27:25.860
bringing up additional VMs
which were preempted earlier.

00:27:25.860 --> 00:27:29.670
So if you needed to complete
the project, no problem.

00:27:29.670 --> 00:27:33.390
Through the automations, even
though Google infrastructure

00:27:33.390 --> 00:27:38.430
